 replacement Ready, and the admission margin before clearing commercial recovery
 or emitting reset completion.
 
+[Recovery launcher ownership](../../PixelStreaming/Docs/recovery-launcher-ownership.md)
+owns the implemented launch-attempt lease and remaining acceptance gates.
+The install-base lifecycle mutex serializes entry, cancellation, replacement
+reservation and actual Node/Unreal spawn. The durable attempt UUID and exact
+PID/creation/executable pins fence late producers and scheduler retries;
+dispatch also binds the helper nonce to the verified source Node birth. These
+identities do not replace API/session generation, ticket cutoff, recovery hold,
+replacement Ready, exact reset acknowledgement or media evidence.
+
+Before revocation, a coherent bundle must arm an independent operation monitor
+and durably bind its identity to the helper, operation, dispatch and planned
+replacement attempt. The monitor cannot repeat cleanup or declare Ready. At its
+deadline (about 601 seconds at default waits), the same marker/lease tuple and
+absence of both pinned and unclassified
+portable runtime Node processes are required under the spawn mutex before a
+durable `stopping` fence and local OS shutdown. Same-boot monitor death cannot
+reopen that fence; normal entry needs positive fresh-boot proof and dead actors.
+The exact tiny native CMD producer is cancelled before final Node/whole-marker
+rechecks; ambiguous invocation or discovery never authorizes arbitrary CMD kills.
+An exact native launcher in another runtime root also denies host-wide shutdown;
+it does not authorize cleanup outside the captured root.
+Normal marker completion/removal or supersession ends monitoring without action.
+A completed lease with a live pinned Node can hand off early; a starting pin
+alone cannot. At the deadline a live Node retains existing agent authority.
+Ambiguous state, an unclassified Node or an unavailable mutex denies shutdown;
+this is not an unconditional stop deadline or a supervisor for a live but hung
+agent or loss of both helpers.
+An unregistered scoped Node also denies every entry write before config/health
+side effects, even after monitor retirement; the Node and lease are preserved.
+Only ungranted repair with exact current pins may retain the same generation.
+
+Maintenance captures the physical source and direct starting-CMD child before
+activation. Lexical invocation plus exact PID/birth/executable keeps the live
+source pin valid after junction retarget. Under the same mutex, no source/target
+Node or latent native producer may remain before revocation and a mode-bound
+exact target CMD reservation. Failure keeps the old generation revoked.
+Terminal BAT paths exit before telemetry CALL after retarget; update failure
+keeps its delayed-stop/hold behavior, while provisioning keeps its bounded
+retry/task-failure behavior. Neither may resume a revoked source launch.
+Installer pruning retains the captured physical source release; uncertain lease
+state skips pruning. Legacy bundles without either lease helper remain explicitly
+unclaimed validation launches with generation cleared and existing validation/
+provider-stop requirements. Partial helper pairs are rejected.
+Leased Git-to-artifact relocation is currently rejected before handoff mutation;
+its captured physical root no longer identifies the archived source. A separate
+pre-activation migration protocol remains required before accepting that route.
+
+Local Windows process fixtures exercise the exclusion/failure protocol with
+fake shutdown. Scoped Dev evidence additionally covers exclusive cold recovery,
+unchanged admission/reset acknowledgement, usable media and a harmless retry of
+the healthy completed stack. One exact recycler loss after revocation was followed
+by observed Node absence, a still-live bound monitor and unchanged intent/lease.
+At the default deadline, its matching fault record and Windows shutdown request
+correlated with independently observed EC2 stopped state. An OS event alone does
+not identify a unique caller, and Node absence is not full producer quiescence.
+The retained-state fresh boot preserved the original operation and cutoff,
+reclaimed ownership, traversed the existing replacement acknowledgement branch
+and delivered usable media without manufacturing state or Ready. Normal End
+and actual provider stop were subsequently observed.
+
+The exact Dev candidate-to-legacy rollback and reapply both passed maintenance
+validation and actual provider stop, with complete retained ownership bytes and
+allowlisted startup journals. Rollback retained the candidate source in sampled
+pointer snapshots; its legacy target stayed intentionally unclaimed and reused
+one Shipping process across two Node births. Reapply completed the candidate
+owner/Node lease and captured candidate-owned native ancestry. The old legacy
+installer nevertheless pruned its source while its exact CMD/updater were alive.
+Its source journal recorded helper terminal code 10 and no later startup phases;
+sampled disappearance does not prove exact caller exit or every old BAT layout.
+Candidate retention/terminal handling cannot retrofit an already running legacy
+installer. This observed pair does not establish general migration compatibility.
+
+A fresh ordinary request after reapply reached API Ready in 111.1013 seconds,
+delivered a sampled 30 fps stream with over 147 seconds of playback, and completed
+normal End with independent actual provider stop. These observations validate
+this scoped Dev behavior, not every failure window or broader hosted acceptance.
+Keep the candidate confined to Dev. Wider promotion remains blocked pending an
+explicit legacy migration step protecting the physical source until its launcher
+and updater exit and preventing old BAT continuation through a retargeted file.
+Validate that path against each environment's actual installed legacy version,
+exact actor births, retained source/target journals, native media and provider stop.
+Leased Git-to-artifact relocation needs its separate pre-activation design.
+
+Deploy only coherent immutable artifacts from stopped, explicitly scoped targets;
+do not trust-migrate a live unleased Node. Stage/Prod additionally require their
+compatible API/artifact, authorized rollout, environment acceptance and rollback
+gates. Neither local fixtures nor scoped Dev evidence close all failure timings,
+prove shutdown with ambiguous actors, or supervise a live but hung agent. Manual
+operator actions, unknown concurrent runtimes and loss of both helpers remain
+outside the proven boundary; ambiguity must preserve admission/shutdown fences.
+API/Web recovery-fault messaging and time estimates remain separate follow-up
+work; this reliability iteration does not change their lifecycle authority.
+
